WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.434
The UK must

00:00:01.246 --> 00:00:02.283
admit its secret

00:00:02.095 --> 00:00:03.097
order to Apple

00:00:03.630 --> 00:00:04.467
For years the

00:00:04.279 --> 00:00:05.446
UK would neither

00:00:05.257 --> 00:00:06.542
confirm nor deny

00:00:06.354 --> 00:00:07.474
issuing Apple a

00:00:07.286 --> 00:00:08.512
Technical Capability

00:00:08.323 --> 00:00:09.726
Notice over encrypted

00:00:09.538 --> 00:00:10.469
iCloud data

00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:12.251
These secret orders

00:00:12.063 --> 00:00:14.173
come under Section 253

00:00:13.985 --> 00:00:15.176
of the Investigatory

00:00:14.988 --> 00:00:17.181
Powers Act 2016

00:00:17.382 --> 00:00:18.100
which let the

00:00:17.912 --> 00:00:18.973
government require

00:00:18.785 --> 00:00:19.787
tech companies to

00:00:19.599 --> 00:00:20.883
change their services

00:00:21.061 --> 00:00:21.956
while keeping the

00:00:21.804 --> 00:00:23.230
order itself secret

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:25.153
Now the Investigatory

00:00:24.965 --> 00:00:26.415
Powers Tribunal has

00:00:26.226 --> 00:00:27.358
ruled the government

00:00:27.170 --> 00:00:28.325
must acknowledge it

00:00:28.526 --> 00:00:29.716
after Liberty and

00:00:29.528 --> 00:00:31.061
Privacy International

00:00:30.873 --> 00:00:32.275
challenged the secrecy

00:00:32.814 --> 00:00:33.828
Full story on

00:00:33.639 --> 00:00:34.535
the dashboard
